{{!--
  Not the shape of THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt -- the raw material for it.

  cargo-about hands its crate lists out in whatever order it happened to find
  them on disk, which is not the same order on two machines. That is invisible
  in a file people only read, and fatal to `notices.ps1 -Check`, which compares
  the generated text against the committed one and cannot tell "a dependency
  changed" from "the same crates came back shuffled". Handlebars cannot sort,
  so this emits one tagged line per fact and tools/notices.ps1 does the sorting
  and the laying out. None of these markers reach the finished file; a license
  whose text contains one stops the run.
--}}
{{#each licenses}}
@@LICENSE@@{{{name}}}
{{#each used_by}}
@@CRATE@@{{{crate.name}}}|{{{crate.version}}}|{{{crate.repository}}}
{{/each}}
@@TEXT@@
{{{text}}}
@@END@@
{{/each}}
